      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know the exact difference between them, but just by seeing the code, makeSupportedSettings adds the attributes to mSupportedValues, which is retrieved by supportsSetting(), and makeSettings adds the attributes to mSettings, which is retrieved by getSetting(). \n\nFrom reading the docStrings, I believe mSupportedValues shows what settings are supported by a single attribute Id by mapping Id to array of settings. On the other hand, mSettings is just a direct hash map of attribute ids to settings, showing current settings.",
